--- perf docs
32:The main process, preload, and snapshot worker are bundled by `scripts/build-electron.ts`; `bun run build:app` and `bun run dev:app` run it through `bun run build:electron`.
36:Components style themselves with Tailwind utilities against the tokens in `src/index.css`. Base UI supplies behavior and accessibility for dialogs, tabs, menus and buttons, with no theme of its own. Plain CSS files are kept only where utilities can't reach: `reader.css` and the note editor style HTML they don't render themselves, onboarding runs on keyframes, and Sonner's toasts are styled through its data attributes. Those files sit next to the component that owns them.
44:Defuddle was created for Obsidian Web Clipper and provides cleaned HTML or Markdown plus metadata such as title, author, domain, favicon, image, publication date, and schema.org data. It also exposes configurable extraction steps and a Node bundle.
91:ONNX Runtime is appropriate for Windows CPU/GPU inference. llama.cpp is appropriate for a bundled or downloaded quantized local language model and provides Windows builds and a local server interface.
120:Treat all fetched HTML as untrusted. Sanitize article HTML before rendering, allowlist iframe providers, strip scripts/event handlers/unsafe URLs/untrusted `srcdoc`, keep remote content isolated from Electron's privileged main process, and do not expose arbitrary filesystem or shell commands through the preload bridge.
